WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.272
On this slide, we are focusing on patient variables.

00:00:03.272 --> 00:00:07.967
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:13.977
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:13.977 --> 00:00:17.647
A variable is a meaningful name connected to a value.

00:00:17.647 --> 00:00:21.577
Clear names help the code communicate what the data represents,

00:00:21.577 --> 00:00:26.572
and later calculations can reuse the stored value.

00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:29.652
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:34.222
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:37.562
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:37.562 --> 00:00:42.580
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
